# /analysis/ used to be listed here — the phase write-ups, ignored as local artifacts.
# They are not artifacts. They are the reasoning behind every decision in this
# repository, and the code they describe is meaningless without them: a reader can see
# that MAX_RESEARCH_LOOPS is 1 and not that it was 2 until a matched-pair experiment
# said the loop bought 77 findings nobody cited.
#
# Twelve files, 680 KB, on one machine with no history. The code was backed up and the
# thinking was not. They are tracked now. Binary, so the diffs are useless — the commit
# messages carry what changed, and the generators are alongside them.
#
# The leading-slash lesson still applies to anything added below: without it, a pattern
# matches any directory of that name at any depth. `analysis` once silently excluded
# src/analysis/, so the cost module would never have been committed and a fresh clone
# could not have run the report.
# Superseded hand-score directories, archived when a re-run or a change to the
# blinding invalidates them. Every version is already reachable in history, so a
# second copy under a new name only confuses which one is canonical. Ignored rather
# than left untracked because code_version() reads the whole tree: an untracked file
# makes every subsequent run record itself as produced from a dirty tree.
results/handscore_superseded/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vscode/settings.json
docs/*.png